{
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nobrega8/mbmap-library/main/schema/mbmap-2.schema.json",
  "mbmap": 2,
  "vendor": "Novus",
  "model": "RHT Climate",
  "models": [
    "RHT Climate",
    "RHT Climate WM",
    "RHT Climate DM"
  ],
  "vendor_website": "novus.com.br",
  "description": "Temperature and humidity transmitter (wall and duct mount) with two analog outputs, two alarm outputs, buzzer and Modbus RTU over RS485: temperature, humidity and psychrometric values, min/max, outputs, alarms, forcing and diagnostics",
  "revision": 1,
  "revised": "2026-10-31",
  "firmware": "V1.4x or later",
  "firmware_min": "1.4",
  "source": "Novus RHT Climate WM / DM instruction manual V1.4x I (Portuguese), chapters 7 and 10",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Transmissor RHT Climate, modelos WM e DM - Manual de Instruções",
      "version": "V1.4x I",
      "url": "https://github.com/user-attachments/files/34218934/Manual_Transmissor_RHT_Climate_WM_DM_PT.pdf",
      "note": "linked in issue #93; section 10.1 and the option tables of chapter 7"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Functions 03, 05, 06 and 16; writes with address 0 are broadcast.",
    "Serial defaults: address 1, 19200 bit/s, no parity. The device answers whatever the stop bits are.",
    "32-bit values are two registers, least significant word first; every register is big-endian. Both registers of a 32-bit value must be read or written together.",
    "The measurements are shown with two decimals. Units follow the unit system (register 127): SI (°C, mbar, g/m³, g/kg, kJ/kg) or US (°F, psi, gr/ft³, gr/lb, BTU/lb).",
    "The manual does not give the decimals of the 32-bit output limits and alarm setpoints; this map reads them with two decimals, like the measurements. Their ranges depend on the quantity chosen for the output or alarm.",
    "Settings with an input pair (103-106, 115-118, 135-138, 152-155, 169-172) are copied to the working pair (108-111, 120-123, 145-148, 162-165, 179-182) when in range; out-of-range inputs are flagged in register 343.",
    "Alarm 3 in the register table is the buzzer (models with display).",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "protocol": "rtu",
  "unit_id": 1,
  "baudrate": 19200,
  "databits": 8,
  "parity": "N",
  "stopbits": 1,
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "little",
  "address_base": 0,
  "x_status": "official",
  "enums": {
    "quantity": {
      "1": "Temperature",
      "2": "Relative humidity",
      "3": "Dew point",
      "4": "Wet bulb temperature",
      "5": "Absolute humidity",
      "6": "Frost point",
      "7": "Specific enthalpy",
      "8": "Vapor partial pressure",
      "9": "Mixing ratio"
    },
    "quantity_off": {
      "0": "Off",
      "1": "Temperature",
      "2": "Relative humidity",
      "3": "Dew point",
      "4": "Wet bulb temperature",
      "5": "Absolute humidity",
      "6": "Frost point",
      "7": "Specific enthalpy",
      "8": "Vapor partial pressure",
      "9": "Mixing ratio"
    },
    "no_yes": {
      "0": "No",
      "1": "Yes"
    },
    "alarm_function": {
      "0": "Off",
      "1": "Sensor error",
      "2": "Below low setpoint",
      "3": "Above high setpoint",
      "4": "Between setpoints",
      "5": "Outside setpoints"
    }
  },
